# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Balu Tools — environment
#
#  Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the site runs
#  completely: every browser-based tool works, and the tools that need a
#  provider render an explicit "Setup required" panel naming the variable
#  it needs.
#
#  SECURITY: never prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Anything with that
#  prefix is inlined into the JavaScript bundle and readable by anyone
#  who opens the page.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical origin. Used for metadata, sitemap.xml, robots.txt and share links.
# Without it, metadata falls back to https://balu.tools.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://balu.tools

# ── AI provider ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works: OpenAI, Groq, Together, OpenRouter,
# Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM. Setting AI_API_KEY enables all 12 AI tools.
#
# AI_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# AI_IMAGE_MODEL=

# ── Server-dependent tools ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PDF encrypt / decrypt. Implemented by YOUR endpoint at
#   POST /api/tools/pdf/encrypt  and  POST /api/tools/pdf/decrypt
# PDF_ENCRYPTION_API_KEY=

# Speech-to-text. Implemented by YOUR endpoint at
#   POST /api/tools/audio/transcribe
# TRANSCRIPTION_API_KEY=

# ── Submissions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tool requests and contact messages. Without these they are validated and
# accepted but held in memory, and lost on restart.
#
# TOOL_REQUESTS_ENDPOINT=https://your-service.example
# TOOL_REQUESTS_TOKEN=
# CONTACT_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://your-service.example/contact
# CONTACT_FORM_TOKEN=

# ── Admin access ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# /admin is COMPLETELY CLOSED until one of these is set. There is no default
# password, so a fresh clone cannot be brute-forced.
#
# ADMIN_SECRET=          # bearer token / cookie must match
# AUTH_SECRET=           # enables signed session cookies

# ── Persistence ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables the sync + usage-analytics adapter in lib/admin/usage.ts.
# The adapter is not shipped — this is the hook point for it.
#
# DATABASE_URL=

# ── Payments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plans and entitlement checks are implemented; the provider adapter is not.
# Checkout refuses with `not_configured` until a provider is registered.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF unless set. Receives toolId → open-count pairs. No identifiers, no
# filenames, no input content, no cookies.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT=

# ── Social links (placeholders until you set them) ──────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_GITHUB=https://github.com/your-org/balu-tools
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_YOUTUBE=https://youtube.com/@yourchannel
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_INSTAGRAM=https://instagram.com/yourhandle
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_X=https://x.com/yourhandle
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@example.com

# ── Advanced ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sets Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy / Embedder-Policy headers, which ffmpeg.wasm
# needs for SharedArrayBuffer. Only enable if you deploy such a tool — the
# headers break cross-origin embeds everywhere else.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CROSS_ORIGIN_ISOLATED=false
